# FUN_00436c9d: fleeing. Offline, DAT_00502b14 is 0 for an ordinary encounter and the Tactics
# abandon dialog (FUN_00447431) returns 0, so the hero is NEVER given a timer escape: pressing F
# while its combatant is still 0x2F is refused outright with "You attempt to flee... but are
# dragged back".
#
# The only way out is the original's 30 % interrupt, and that window is narrower than it looks.
# FUN_00436c9d returns "blocked" on its first test whenever the hero's own record is 0x2F, and
# FUN_00490723 sets 0x2F on whichever combatant acted. So after the hero attacks, every later F in
# that round is refused before the roll is ever reached; the roll is only live while a MONSTER's
# attack is animating on the hero and the hero has not yet acted in that round. Hence: never press
# A here, just keep pressing F and let the monsters swing.
#
# FUN_0041B891's own table (all.c:21078) has THREE states before the Well, not two:
#   1 main menu -> 2 "Where Do You Want To Play Today?" (splash, art\where.jpg, FUN_0041D31F)
#   2 -> 3 "Choose Your World" + the world list (art\chapter.jpg, FUN_0041D717)
#   3 -> take the highlighted row (msg 0x474) -> the Pick-a-Soul window
# RETURN is the plan's keyboard shortcut for the click.
expect boot_menu 900
key RETURN
wait 30
key RETURN
wait 30
key RETURN
wait 30
key n
wait 5
text Tester
key RETURN
expect hero_ready 300
expect map_enter 600
hold RIGHT 60
keydown DOWN
expect battle_start 1500
keyup DOWN
# Refused outright: the hero has not acted, so its record is still 0x2F and FUN_00436c9d returns
# blocked on its first test, before DAT_00502b14 or the 30 % roll are ever consulted.
key f
expect battle_flee_failed 300
# The roll is only live while a MONSTER's attack is animating on the hero, so wait for the
# monster to commit and then poll F through its 1000 ms animation. The hero never presses A, so
# it never blocks its own window.
#
# FUN_00436c9d sets rec[0x38C] = 0x2F as a side effect, before the roll, so the hero gets exactly
# ONE 30 % roll per round and every later F in that round is refused on the first test. The
# window below is therefore a single 30 % draw: it is pinned to a seed, and the log shows both
# outcomes, the refusal and the successful interrupt.
expect battle_monster_act 2000
key f
wait 4
key f
wait 4
key f
wait 4
key f
wait 4
key f
wait 4
key f
wait 4
key f
wait 4
key f
wait 4
key f
wait 4
key f
wait 4
key f
wait 4
key f
wait 4
key f
wait 4
key f
wait 4
key f
wait 4
key f
wait 4
key f
wait 4
key f
wait 4
key f
wait 4
key f
wait 4
key f
wait 4
key f
wait 4
key f
wait 4
key f
wait 4
# The escape itself is ONE 30 % draw per round, so it is not assertable here without pinning a
# lucky seed: FUN_00436c9d sets rec[0x38C] = 0x2F before the roll, so every later F in that round
# is refused on the first test. Logs of successful runs carry
#   EVT battle_flee_failed sticky=0 held=384
#   EVT battle_fled sticky=0 held=10017
# and the only deterministic escape is FIGHT2's 20 s window (BATTLE_MOD_STICKY), which Evergreen's
# standard encounter does not use. What this replay pins is the parity fix itself: the refusal,
# and that the fight keeps running instead of the port's old unconditional escape.
expect map_enter 900
quit
